<title>HONG KONG: ITC mulls buying CEF Concord stake.</title>
<headline>ITC mulls buying CEF Concord stake.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Civil engineering group International Tak Chueng Holdings Ltd (ITC) said on Wednesday it was holding preliminary negotiations with CEF Concord Holdings Ltd which might result in a reorganisation, but it gave no details.</p>
<p>Construction company CEF Concord is 51 percent held by Fortune Leader Ltd, a company which in turn is held approximately 12.1 percent by Paul Y-ITC Construction Holdings Ltd. Paul Y-ITC is 35.6 percent held by ITC.</p>
<p>CEF Concord gained five H.K. cents to HK$1.08 while ITC lost two cents to $1.91 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
